  "$comment": "The ten sponsor categories of SPEC §5.3 S10, keyed by the contracts SponsorCategory enum; a run uses at most six. Names, query strings and public taxonomy URNs only (D29). semantic_query is the /v2/tags semantic search (filter.parents.types=urn:entity:brand) that finds each category's tags at runtime; probe gate G14 matched it for the eight categories marked G14, telecom and fintech were not probed. G14 returned mostly descriptive *:qloo:* tags, which are not taste signals. The P5 probe verified both a urn:tag:product_category:qloo:* tag and a urn:tag:genre:brand:* leaf as filter.tags on brand insights (20/20 results carry the tag; verified_as brand_filter, never a signal), so tags lists the filter tag P5 exercised and stays empty for the other categories until one is verified. Several filter.tags values combine as a union (P5: 20/20 rows carried either energy tag, 9/20 both), so each category lists one tag and S10 sends one category per call. aliases help CLERK and the command grammar map question words to a category.",
